    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 1994, amending chapter 285 of the\nlaws of 1891 relating to charging a fee for admission to the New York\nBotanical Garden, in relation to making permanent certain provisions\nauthorizing the imposition of a required fee; and to repeal section 2 of such\nchapter 465 of the laws of 1994 relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S4449",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4449-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 38,
       "fullName": "David Carlucci",
       "imgName": "370_david_carlucci.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 370,
       "sessionMemberId": 1191,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "CARLUCCI"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, rpld §2, Chap 465 of 1994",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4449\n\nSPONSOR: BIAGGI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 1994,\namending chapter 285 of the laws of 1891 relating to charging a fee for\nadmission to the New York Botanical Garden, in relation to making perma-\nnent certain provisions authorizing the imposition of a required fee;\nand to repeal section 2 of such chapter 465 of the laws of 1994 relating\nthereto\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to give the New York Botanical Garden\nauthorization to charge or not charge an admission fee.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends chapter 465 of the laws of 1994, section 3 and subse-\nquent extensions, to eliminate the expiration date authorizing the New\nYork Botanical Garden to charge a fee for admission by the general\npublic to help sustain the organization's operations and botanical\nexhibits.\n\nSection 2:\n\nSection 3: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York Botanical Garden (NYBG) charges nominal and varying fees\nfor admission to certain exhibits of this organization. They must be\nauthorized to continue to do so in order to remain open to the public\nand a financially viable organization that can continue to host new\nliving exhibits. This legislation will provide NYBG with parity among\nother organizations that are not required to pass legislation yearly to\ncharge admission.\n\nThe following organizations charge for admission and do not require\nlegislation to do so:\n\nBronx\n\nBronx Academy of Arts and Dance\n\nBronx River Arts Center\n\nLehman Center for the Performing Arts\n\nHostos Center for Performing Arts\n\nPregones Theater\n\nWave Hill\n\nManhattan\n\nAmerican Museum of Natural History\n\nCarnegie Hall\nEl Museo del Barrio\n\nLincoln Center for the Performing Arts\n\nMoMa\n\nMetropolitan Museum of Art\n\nMetropolitan Opera\n\nMuseum of the City of New York\n\nNew York City Ballet\n\nNew York Historical Society\n\nNew York Philharmonic\n\nPublic Theater\n\nStudio Museum in Harlem\n\nGuggenheim\n\nThe Whitney\n\nBrooklyn\n\nBrooklyn Academy of Music (BAN) Brooklyn Children's Museum\n\nBrooklyn Museum\n\nBrooklyn Botanic Garden\n\nNY Aquarium\n\nQueens\n\nFlushing Town Hall\n\nMuseum of the Moving Image\n\nQueens Botanical Garden\n\nQueens Museum Queens Theater\n\nStaten Island\n\nSnug Harbor and Cultural Center\n\nStaten Island Children's Museum Staten\n\nIsland Historical Society Staten Island Museum\n\nStaten Island Zoo\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately\n",
